Saudi civil defence says danger has passed after alerts issued in southern cities






                Saudi Arabia's civil defence authority said that danger passed in several southern cities after alerts were issued.&nbsp;

A while earlier, warning of possible threats were issued in&nbsp;Khamis Mushait, Abha, Taif and Najran.

Saudi-led coalition says it destroyed Houthi missile targeting kingdom's southern region






                The Saudi-led coalition said that its air defences&nbsp;intercepted and destroyed a Houthi ballistic missile that was heading toward Saudi Arabia’s southern region.

Earlier,&nbsp;Saudi Arabia's civil defence authority issued alerts&nbsp;in Khamis Mushait, Abha, Taif and Najran, later announcing that the danger had passed.&nbsp;

Israeli opposition leader Eisenkot says Netanyahu 'failed' to&nbsp;discredit election results






                Israel’s Yashar party leader Gadi Eisenkot said that Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his party "failed" to&nbsp;discredit Israeli election results.&nbsp;

"The vile and malicious attempt to deny the election results, to undermine the will of the public, to smear an entire public, and to drag Israel into additional elections has failed," he said in a post on X.

"Only someone who understands that they have lost would embark on such a brazen campaign of delegitimisation - even at the cost of further eroding public trust in the state's institutions."

He described the recent election results "clear and unequivocal", and urged Israeli citizens to "ignore the background noise".

"The people are sovereign, and they have spoken: the government of failure has no majority and it has lost," he added, referring to Netanyahu's government.&nbsp;

Israeli forces have withdrawn from Hebron, governor says






                The governor of Hebron said that Israeli forces withdrew from the occupied West Bank city following a nearly two weeks-long operation.&nbsp;

Khaled Dudin told Al Jazeera that Palestinian security forces are now in complete control of the area, adding that families who were forced to leave their homes are now able to return.
